---
description: Use Context7 for current library and API documentation
alwaysApply: true
---

When the user asks about library APIs, framework setup, or code examples from an external package, use Context7 instead of relying on training data.

Prefer the Context7 MCP tools (`resolve-library-id`, then `query-docs`). If MCP is unavailable, use the `ctx7` CLI:

```
npx ctx7 library <name> "<query>"
npx ctx7 docs <libraryId> "<query>"
```

Do not invent APIs. Cite the library and version you used.
